  {
    "id": "GHSA-62m5-6wh8-28x7",
    "summary": "pypdf has possible long runtimes/large memory usage for encrypted PDF files",
    "details": "### Impact\n\nAn attacker who uses this vulnerability can craft a PDF which leads to large runtimes/memory usage. This requires accessing the page count of an encrypted PDF file, which itself declares a wrong `/Count` value.\n\n### Patches\n\nThis has been fixed in [pypdf==6.21.3](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/releases/tag/6.21.3).\n\n### Workarounds\n\nIf you cannot upgrade yet, consider applying the changes from PR [#4270](https://github.com/py-pdf/pypdf/pull/4270).",
